
---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

  <p>
    <strong>BlueGate Labs</strong><br />
    Last updated: 2 November 2026
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>1. Overview</h2>
    <p>
      BlueGate Labs is an independent Australian software development
      and cybersecurity initiative. We respect the privacy of visitors
      and aim to handle personal information responsibly.
    </p>
    <p>
      This policy explains how information may be collected, used
      and disclosed when you visit our website or contact us.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>
      If you contact us by email, we may receive your name,
      email address and any information you choose to provide.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our website does not currently offer user accounts,
      online purchases or contact forms.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our hosting and infrastructure providers may process
      technical information, including IP addresses and request
      details, to operate and protect the website.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>3. How We Use Information</h2>
    <p>Information provided through correspondence may be used to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Respond to enquiries and support requests.</li>
      <li>Discuss projects and potential collaboration.</li>
      <li>Investigate security or privacy concerns.</li>
      <li>Maintain appropriate business records.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell personal information.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>4. Website Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      BlueGate Labs uses Cloudflare Web Analytics to understand
      website usage and performance. This service provides
      aggregated information about pageviews and visits
      without using cookies or fingerprinting individual visitors.
    </p>
    <p>
      Cloudflare also processes technical request information
      to deliver, secure and monitor the website.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not currently use Google Analytics, Meta Pixel
      or advertising tracking technologies.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>5. Third-Party Service Providers</h2>
    <p>
      Our website uses Cloudflare for hosting, content delivery,
      security and analytics. Our email services are provided
      by VentraIP.
    </p>
    <p>
      These providers may process information as necessary to
      deliver their services, in accordance with their own
      privacy policies and applicable laws.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>6. Information Security</h2>
    <p>
      We take reasonable steps to protect information under
      our control against unauthorised access, misuse and disclosure.
      However, no internet-based system can be guaranteed
      completely secure.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>7. Retention and Access</h2>
    <p>
      We retain correspondence and related records for as long
      as reasonably necessary for their purpose, subject to
      applicable legal obligations.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may contact us to request access to, correction of,
      or deletion of personal information we hold about you.
      Requests will be considered in accordance with applicable law.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>8. Other Software Products</h2>
    <p>
      This policy covers the BlueGate Labs website and related
      correspondence. Individual software products may have
      separate privacy policies describing their specific
      information handling practices.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy to reflect changes to our
      website, services or legal obligations. The latest
      version will be published here.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>10. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy enquiries, contact
      <a href="mailto:privacy@bluegatelabs.au">
        privacy@bluegatelabs.au
      </a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
